=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play users/one-key -------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the User Management screen proposed for$
# slice 5, drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host$
# (users.Admin.Check, users.ReadElevation, sudoers.Read,$
# PolicyOf, Invoker, ssh.ReadPAM), each grant the real$
# sudoers.PlanFor on the real plan/apply engine. Creating a user$
# and the keys are the gallery's stand-ins, unit (b)'s to build.$
# Nothing on this machine changes: every command and file is the$
# fake's.$
$
# Info: users/one-key$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. debian13, but george has$
# one key: removing it is refused. alice has none, and no .ssh.$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
$
# george -------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password$
   -  Granted by           /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users$
   -  SSH Keys             1 key$
   -  Password             None$
$
# alice --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Sudo                 Enabled$
   -  Granted by           group sudo$
  [ ] SSH Keys             None$
   -  Password             Set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Manage User          Configure sudo, SSH keys$
   2) Create User          Configure a new user$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Select a user$
$
   1) george$
   2) alice$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Managing: [george]$
$
# User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password$
   -  Granted by           /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users$
   -  SSH Keys             1 key$
   -  Password             None$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Remove admin rights  Take sudo away$
   2) Ask for password     For sudo$
   3) SSH Keys             Add or remove SSH keys$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-3 or q]: 3$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Managing SSH keys for: [george]$
$
# SSH Keys -----------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  SHA256:RXm/ruZ0eTzRXKwi1AQEDynB0VgHQ2ac9KPSFdf/YnA$
      george@laptop-1$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Add SSH key$
   2) Remove SSH key$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 2$
$
# Warning$
# This is george's last key, and you're logged in as george. Add$
# another key first.$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Managing SSH keys for: [george]$
$
# SSH Keys -----------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  SHA256:RXm/ruZ0eTzRXKwi1AQEDynB0VgHQ2ac9KPSFdf/YnA$
      george@laptop-1$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Add SSH key$
   2) Remove SSH key$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Managing: [george]$
$
# User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password$
   -  Granted by           /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users$
   -  SSH Keys             1 key$
   -  Password             None$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Remove admin rights  Take sudo away$
   2) Ask for password     For sudo$
   3) SSH Keys             Add or remove SSH keys$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-3 or q]: 0$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Select a user$
$
   1) george$
   2) alice$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
$
# george -------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password$
   -  Granted by           /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users$
   -  SSH Keys             1 key$
   -  Password             None$
$
# alice --------------------------------------------------------$
